Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:13.600 align:start position:0%
 
beer  I'm in Rotterdam on my way to the  biggest and busiest harbour in Europe  every day hundreds of vessels sail in  carrying cargo from all over the world  I've come here to meet a young man who  works on board a cargo vessel this is  urine right now he's in the middle of  his shift  cleaning out old fuel from the ship's  fuel tanks  Jeroen is 20 years old than a Seafarer  from the netherlands  he's an apprentice onboard the vessel  and he's studying for a career as a  ship's officer  but right now he's still learning and  has to do everything including the dirty  stuff  the ship just arrived here in Rotterdam  after a week's journey on the ocean  walking on board feels like I'm entering  a different world ships like these are  much longer than a soccer field and can  carry thousands of tons of cargo I get  to talk to you rune during a break I'm  curious if he knows what happens when  ships like these die and end up in ship  breaking yards in the developing world  so I do know what's going on in those  countries and it's really kind of  ridiculous you know that  with the with the technology of today  and safety equipment and everything it  still has to go in such a way because  it's just cheaper you know  the people walking barefoot and  and everything is as just sad you know  before they go to the ship breaking  yards these big vessels can live up to  30 years they handle a huge amount of  the world's train around 90% of the  world's stuff is transported by ship  after work we go inside the boats to the  sleeping quarters urine shows me his  room where he's living for his  five-month shift on board it looks  comfortable he has an ocean view and a  private bathroom but I do notice that  something's missing there's no posters  or pictures on the walls to remind him  of his friends and family leaving them  behind doesn't seem easy you told me  that you didn't sleep very well last  night  wait was it at all because you were  thinking about your girlfriend or was it  just something different yeah sometimes  you worry a bit about things like like  how do I do this or how do we do that  and how is it going with my girlfriend  and my family and you know what are my  friends doing at this place at the right  moment you know are they having a party  or maybe hanging out and a lot of things  which I miss you know because I just  can't be there because I'm on the ship  and yeah sometimes you can worry about  it but yeah I try not to think about it  too much  hmmm hello Jeroen sends text messages to  his girlfriend every day but he hasn't  seen her since the day he came on board  three months ago the next day Jeroen and  the crew are preparing for a ship  inspection they need to make sure  everything works perfectly  today the engine is getting a tune-up  your rune helps lift it out of the room  below the engine is heavy and fragile  there are only 12 men working on the  ship so there's plenty of work to go  around  sometimes even the seafarers need a  tune-up after a long day of work this is  where they come to work out their  frustrations it's the craziest gym I've  ever seen everything is made from old  boat parts including the bench press he  lets me give it a try  you see it's not that bad you have a bad  day just work out and forget everything  that's  your rooms coworker Oliver is from the  Philippines one out of every five  seafarers in the world is from there  when your room gets a full time job  he'll work for about three months with  no break but most Filipinos work for a  year or more non-stop to send money to  their families I have the biggest  respect for these guys that they can  manage it to do it and every day they  even if it's raining -20° thick layer of  ice on the ship and you know and still  they're working and that for eight  months straight yeah it's really crazy I  think for us in Europe it's it's almost  unthinkable to do this kind of work for  that small amount of money which they  get  your ruins job isn't really popular with  young people  right now more than half a million  people work as ships officers but 20,000  jobs are open and that number is  expected to increase the shipping  industry thinks young people aren't  interested in a physically demanding job  where they'll be away from home for  months at a time but hanging out with  your rune it's clear to me that he  enjoys it even through the tough times  soon the ship will leave Rotterdam to  sail again to the next port do are you  ever afraid you ever think about there  being an accident on the ship or  something dangerous happen  I'm not afraid but you have to keep it  really in mind because there's always a  possibility that something goes wrong  you know and and it's quite dangerous  there are so many things that can happen  if you see what we're lifting and with  what weights we're working and what  amounts of cargo you know the dangers of  the cargo the dangers of sailing on a  ship you know if you're in the middle of  the ocean and something happens to the  ship yeah you know it's it's quite  dangerous for example no more and I'm  where we're standing right now if it  snaps yeah we won't be standing here  tomorrow how long do you think you want  to do this for maybe when I got children  I want to quit and a search for a job  ashore you know but maybe I will do this  for the rest of my life until I retire  or go down with the ship you know it's  yeah  you

